T15:18:35.579Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e"}
{"parentUuid":"88e3bb3b-8cfa-48fb-845b-2571b25d91b0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a7e54ea3099505a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YUqCDYSTdEvzhnCBj69juQ","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nconcern: the size of Go files\nsloprails: [gate/file-size, file-guard/file-size]\nlimits:\n  go: 150         # non-test Go\n  go_test: 400    # *_test.go\n# Legacy files over their limit, and the most lines each may hold. A ceiling\n# only goes down; a file under its limit leaves the list.\nceilings:\n  claude-mock/internal/runner/runner.go: 179            # Run alone is ~163\n  claude-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go: 164   # compact alone is ~151\n  claude-mock/internal/runner/stream_turn.go: 152       # runOneTurnSig alone is ~140\n---\n\n# Go files stay small\n\n## Concern\n\nThe size of every Go file in the repository.\n\n## Decision\n\n- A non-test Go file has at most `limits.go` lines. A test file has at most\n  `limits.go_test` lines.\n- A file listed under `ceilings` holds at most its ceiling.\n- New code is split by responsibility into files within the limit.\n---\nconcern: which packages core and the harness mocks may import\nsloprails: [file-guard/layering, file-guard/adr-conformance]\n---\n\n# One shared core; harness mocks depend on it, never on each other\n\n## Concern\n\nPackage imports between `internal/` and the per-harness mocks.\n\n## Decision\n\n- No package under `internal/` imports a package under any `*-mock/`.\n- No package under `<a>-mock/` imports a package under a different\n  `<b>-mock/`. It imports only `internal/` and its own packages.\n- Code two mocks both need lives in the repo-root `internal/`.\n- A harness's adapter (its wire format, record shapes, CLI) lives in its own\n  mock, under `<harness>-mock/internal/`.\ncommit f860ff366b50328d62a3ff06a1cd76d39e84245f\nAuthor: Mykyta Svyrydenko <<redacted-email>>\nDate:   Sat Oct 3 16:44:15 2026 +0200\n\n    codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\n    \n    Codex tells the agent a failed command's output like a success's; the failure is only in the event stream's command_execution item (status failed, exit_code). Recorded with the real codex; the cell lists that as a deviation, and the mock does the same.\n    \n    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/shell_result_test.go b/codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/shell_result_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..5a69d73\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/shell_result_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@\n+package e2e\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\"\n+\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n+)\n+\n+// The recorded run runs/shell-exit-status: commands exiting 1 with no output,\n+// 1 with output, 2 with both streams, 3 with none, and 0.\n+\n+// A shell command's result is its output and a structured form of it, the\n+// stream's command_execution item: its exit code, what the command printed\n+// (both streams, interleaved) and a status, \"failed\" for any non-zero exit\n+// (grep finding nothing included) and \"completed\" for 0. The agent is told\n+// the output alone, the same for a failure as for a success: no exit code,\n+// no error mark (runs/shell-exit-status).\n+// sr:proves bash-tool-result/codex\n+func TestShellResultIsOutputAndItsStructuredForm(t *testing.T) {\n+\trec := loadRecording(t, \"shell-exit-status\")\n+\t// the commands the model asked for, as the recorded hooks saw them\n+\trec.calls = nil\n+\tfor _, p := range jsonLines(readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.sample, \"payloads.jsonl\"))) {\n+\t\tif in, ok := p[\"tool_input\"].(map[string]any); ok && p[\"hook_event_name\"] == \"PostToolUse\" {\n+\t\t\trec.calls = append(rec.calls, in[\"command\"].(string))\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\trequire.Len(t, rec.calls, 5)\n+\tgot := replay(t, rec)\n+\trequire.Equal(t, 0, got.Code, got.Stderr)\n+\n+\titems := func(r result) (out []map[string]any) {\n+\t\tfor _, e := range r.stream() {\n+\t\t\tif item, _ := e[\"item\"].(map[string]any); e[\"type\"] == \"item.completed\" && item[\"type\"] == \"command_execution\" {\n+\t\t\t\tout = append(out, map[string]any{\n+\t\t\t\t\t\"output\": item[\"aggregated_output\"], \"exit\": item[\"exit_code\"], \"status\": item[\"status\"]})\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\twant := items(result{Stdout: readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.sample, \"stream.jsonl\"))})\n+\trequire.Len(t, want, 5)\n+\tassert.Equal(t, want, items(got))\n+\n+\t// PostToolUse fires after every one of them, failed or not, with the\n+\t// output as the response: the same payloads the recording holds\n+\tvar wantPost, gotPost []map[string]any\n+\tfor _, l := range jsonLines(readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.sample, \"payloads.jsonl\"))) {\n+\t\tif l[\"hook_event_name\"] == \"PostToolUse\" {\n+\t\t\twantPost = append(wantPost, l)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, l := range got.hookLog() {\n+\t\tif l[\"hook_event_name\"] == \"PostToolUse\" {\n+\t\t\tgotPost = append(gotPost, l)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\trequire.Len(t, wantPost, 5)\n+\tassert.Equal(t, sortedHookLines(wantPost), sortedHookLines(gotPost))\n+\n+\tbyExit := map[float64]string{}\n+\tfor _, it := range items(got) {\n+\t\tbyExit[it[\"exit\"].(float64)] = it[\"status\"].(string)\n+\t}\n+\tassert.Equal(t, map[float64]string{0: \"completed\", 1: \"failed\", 2: \"failed\", 3: \"failed\"}, byExit)\n+\n+\trollout := got.rollout(t)\n+\tassert.True(t, resultTold(t, rollout, \"MORE-OUTPUT\\nERR-OUTPUT\", \"xit code\"), \"the output of a failed command, and no exit code\")\n+\tassert.True(t, resultTold(t, rollout, \"FINE\", \"xit code\"))\n+}\ninternal/hooks/match.go:29:func Matches(matcher, value string, aliases ...string) bool {\ninternal/hooks/match.go-30-\treturn Select(MatchRegexp, matcher, value, aliases...)\ninternal/hooks/match.go-31-}\ninternal/hooks/match.go-32-\ninternal/hooks/match.go-33-// Select reports whether a hook's matcher selects the subject its event\ninternal/hooks/match.go-34-// filters on (the tool name for a tool event, how a session started for a\ninternal/hooks/match.go-35-// session-start event): an empty matcher or \"*\" selects everything; any other\ninternal/hooks/match.go-36-// is read as the style says, against the subject and each of its aliases\ninternal/hooks/match.go-37-// (other names a harness gives the same tool). A matcher that is not a regular\ninternal/hooks/match.go-38-// expression selects nothing.\ninternal/hooks/match.go-39-//\ninternal/hooks/match.go-40-// sr:capability hook-matcher-filter\ninternal/hooks/match.go-41-func Select(style MatcherStyle, matcher, subject string, aliases ...string) bool {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7063a73a-5f6d-4ffa-b2f0-299f873b7984","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:18:39.172Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"88e3bb3b-8cfa-48fb-845b-2571b25d91b0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e"}
