{"parentUuid":"ef825e00-0235-4307-b986-e4403bb47b42","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a7e54ea3099505a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QLHxnFNhSsZJBmjkwKypiV","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - TestHookAddedContextIsKept covers only SessionStart source=startup, plain and JSON context from SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse plain text ignored, PostToolUse JSON kept, and two UserPromptSubmit hooks. Several behaviours in the hooks doc have no test and no declared deviation. SessionStart context on source resume, clear and compact is not tested (doc lines 656 and 674-679, including delivery to the continuation after mid-turn compaction). additionalContext from an async background hook, delivered at the next model request (doc lines 619-630), is not tested. No test checks that SessionStart context from several hooks is all kept, or that PostToolUse context from several hooks is all kept. Only UserPromptSubmit is checked for multiple hooks.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/subagent_stop_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/agent_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/stderr.txt (and 19 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The only test, TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd, replays just runs/stops and checks that the Stop events number 3, that the two reason strings appear anywhere in the rollout, and that there is one turn.completed. The codex doc (Stop section) says the reason becomes a new user prompt, but no test checks that the reason is handed back as a user-role prompt, so a mock that only logged the text would pass. The doc also says a Stop hook returning `continue: false` takes precedence over block decisions, and no test or run covers that. The recorded hook-exit-codes run, where a single exit-2 stderr reason is followed by an allowed stop, is not exercised by any test.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/subagent_stop_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/agent_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/samples/20261003-151437/stderr.txt (and 19 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing pins last_assistant_message to \"DONE\", but every recorded Stop payload in runs/stops (e.g. {\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"stop_hook_active\":false}) has no last_assistant_message or turn_id field, so the test contradicts the recording; the doc's null-when-unavailable case for last_assistant_message and the turn_id field are also untested.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/subagent_stop_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/agent_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-b