{"parentUuid":"eeb9ef54-7e85-40ea-842b-78b5a907874f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7e54ea3099505a7e","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffcj4mymMEkvVh4QWfZE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the cursor cell, and the codex cell is built and tested locally, but nothing is pushed: the verify-before-push gate blocks it. One `sr-checks` refusal remains, a gap in another capability's coverage that my edit to `codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go` makes the judges re-judge.\n\n**Cells in `spec/capabilities/subagent-stop-block-loop.yaml`**\n- **codex: supported.** The run `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop` shows the real `codex` doing it. The `SubagentStop` hook blocked twice, once by a JSON decision and once by exit 2, then let the sub-agent stop. Each block's reason sits in the sub-agent's own rollout as a `<hook_prompt>` user message, and the parent session's rollout holds none of it. The cell cites the frozen hooks doc at `#subagentstop`.\n- **codex deviations, both `modeled-surface`:**\n  - The mock sets no block cap, because the recording never reached one.\n  - The mock does not read a hook's `continue:false`, which the docs say outranks a block.\n  - It also models only a sub-agent that speaks, with no tool calls or nested/background sub-agents, and only `spawn_agent`, not the model's own `wait`.\n- **cursor: unsupported.** The run `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/subagent-stop-block-loop` (captured with the 2026.09.28 build on PATH) shows the sub-agent ran and answered `SUBDONE`. Neither the `subagentStart` nor the `subagentStop` hook fired, so only `sessionStart` appears in the payloads. The cell cites that run, with no docs.\n\n**What I implemented (codex)**\n- A `spawn_agent` tool in the mock, run on the shared core `subagents.Execute`.\n- Events and hooks in codex-mock:\n  - `agent_host.go` and `agent_hooks.go` in `codex-mock/internal/runner/`\n  - `collab.go` in `codex-mock/internal/events/`\n  - two new event constants in `codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go`\n- A one-line `agentHost` wrapper in `run.go`.\n- `codex-mock/internal/runner/agent_*.go` added to the home of `internal/subagents/module.yaml`.\n- Three tests marked `sr:proves subagent-stop-block-loop/codex` in `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/subagent_stop_test.go`. They cover the block loop, the sub-agent rollout path with `SessionEnd`, and payload fields plus matcher. They pass, and the other codex-mock and internal tests passed in earlier runs.\n\n**Not merged**\n- **No PR.** Three commits sit on branch `worktree-agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e`.\n- **Remaining refusal.** The `noninteractive-run/codex` judge says no test asserts the two `error` items every recorded run streams, and that `prompt-blocked` is never driven. That is untouched code of another capability. Earlier runs also flagged `session-start-hook/codex` and `hook-additional-context/codex` the same way. Putting the dispatch in `turn_host.go` instead dragged in four more of that kind, so I kept it in `run.go`. The gate blocked my push and I did not work around it.\n- **Decision for you.** Either someone fixes those other capabilities' tests (or declares deviations), or a push is authorised despite the refusal. The cursor cell does not depend on any of this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1159,"cache_read_input_tokens":189377,"output_tokens":1426,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":234},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1159},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1426,"cache_read_input_tokens":189377,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1159,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1159,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"stand