{"parentUuid":"e7d96238-a40b-4680-99ac-7135b37e057a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a7e54ea3099505a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GZmTWicRTaUrQiCQKkKdAn","type":"tool_result","content":"346\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-covered\" changeset: refused (3/15 settled, 1m11s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"shapes\" changeset: refused (7/15 settled, 1m17s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\" claude: refused (8/15 settled, 1m18s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\" codex: refused (9/15 settled, 1m20s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\" cursor: refused (10/15 settled, 1m21s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-grounded\": its subjects script \"./subjects.sh\" failed: a file under spec/capabilities is not valid YAML: {\"id\":\"agent-input-validation\",\"path\":\"spec/capabilities/agent-input-validation.yaml\",\"doc\":{\"statement\":\"A sub-agent dispatch that lacks its required description or prompt is refused with an input-validation error before any hook runs, and nothing runs.\",\"providers\":{\"claude\":{\"docs\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference#agent-tool-behavior\"],\"runs\":[\"claude-mock/snapshots/runs/agent-invalid-input\",\"claude-mock/snapshots/runs/agent-invalid-descr\n{\"id\":\"file-tools\",\"path\":\"spec/capabilities/file-tools.yaml\",\"doc\":{\"statement\":\"The agent can read and write files in its working directory: a read returns the file's content, a write creates a file or replaces one whole, and a call that fails (a file that is not there) surfaces as an error result. (Numbered lines, offsets and limits, edits of an exact string, globs, images, PDFs and notebooks, files too large for the token limit, the rules that make a file be read before it is changed, and the ignore settings of a glob are not part of this.)\",\"providers\":{\"claude\":{\"docs\":[\"https://code.cla\n{\"id\":\"hook-additional-context\",\"path\":\"spec/capabilities/hook-additional-context.yaml\",\"doc\":{\"statement\":\"A hook run at the start of a session, on a submitted prompt, or after a tool call succeeds can return text that is added to the agent's context (a harness may take it at only some of these); when several hooks return text, all of it is kept. A harness that records what its hooks output records the text beside the hook's own output. (What a harness does with text too long to keep whole is not part of this.)\",\"providers\":{\"claude\":{\"docs\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#add-context\n{\"id\":\"hook-common-payload\",\"path\":\"spec/capabilities/hook-common-payload.yaml\",\"doc\":{\"statement\":\"Every lifecycle hook receives a payload naming the session, its transcript file and its working directory. An event raised inside a sub-agent also names that sub-agent, while events on the main thread name none.\",\"providers\":{\"claude\":{\"docs\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#common-input-fields\"],\"runs\":[\"claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookmix\",\"claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\"]},\"codex\":{\"docs\":[\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#common-input-fields\"],\"runs\":[\"codex-mock/snapshots/r\n{\"id\":\"hook-exit-code-semantics\",\"path\":\"spec/capabilities/hook-exit-code-semantics.yaml\",\"doc\":{\"statement\":\"A hook command's exit status classifies its outcome: accepted (0), blocked (2, with the hook's stderr as its message when it gave no other reason), or a non-blocking error (any other status, except on WorktreeCreate, where any non-zero status fails the creation, and except, in a harness that reads a hook's output whatever its status, when stdout holds valid JSON, which alone decides the outcome), after which the action goes on, unless the harness has a setting that makes a hook's failu\n{\"id\":\"stop-hook-payload\",\"path\":\"spec/capabilities/stop-hook-payload.yaml\",\"doc\":{\"statement\":\"A hook fires each time the agent finishes responding. Its payload