{"parentUuid":"51744a87-3439-4eb3-8fe7-4ff4573fb0a1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a7e54ea3099505a7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017MmWX6h76M5jAn2APEFkNn","type":"tool_result","content":"[{'adr': 'capability-grounding', 'statement': \"Codex has no block cap for a sub-agent's stop hook; a hook that blocked 15 times in a row had the sub-agent run again each time, so the loop ends only when the hook lets it stop.\"}]\nThe Codex doc for SubagentStop says that if any matching SubagentStop hook returns `continue: false`, it takes precedence over the other hooks' block decisions, so the sub-agent stops instead of running again. No test in codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/subagent_stop_test.go exercises it, and neither recorded run shows it. The other checklist items are covered: block by JSON and by exit 2 with the reasons in the sub-agent's own rollout, `stop_hook_active` flipping to true, the matcher on `agent_type`, `agent_transcript_path`, and the uncapped 15-block deviation. (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n\n[exited with code 0]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"75c17b35-1d20-491b-92a5-15e5f4a9ee6d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:25:11.691Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51744a87-3439-4eb3-8fe7-4ff4573fb0a1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078"}
